    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        640,
        740
      ],
      "size": [
        560,
        430
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 8,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Read me",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "MiniMax H3 S3 + corrector - image to video\n\nLoad your first frame in \"First frame (input image)\" and describe the motion in \"Image to video\". The first frame is resized to width x height, so set them to the same aspect ratio as your image (multiples of 32).\n\nThe model, text encoder, VAEs, corrector, shift 12 / 3, Euler, simple schedule and 20 steps are the same as the text-to-video workflow. S3 is guidance-distilled, so it runs at CFG 1 with BasicGuider and no negative prompt.\n\nApply H3 Corrector runs on every step by default.\n  start_step / end_step: 0-based and inclusive; -1 = through the last step.\n  strength 0 turns it off.\n  budget_fraction 0.5 and velocity_floor 0.001 are what the S3 corrector was trained with.\n\nlength snaps to 17k+5 frames at 24 fps: 56 is about 2 s, 124 about 5 s.\n\nThe S3 pipeline prompts with structured JSON captions, like the example prompt. Keep the subject's appearance consistent with the input image and describe only what moves.\n\nLoadH3Corrector / ApplyH3Corrector come from S3_ComfyUI.zip in the SulphurAI/Sulphur-3 repository. To run without them, bypass both corrector nodes (Ctrl+B)."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "MiniMax H3 S3 + corrector - image to video\n\nLoad your first frame in \"First frame (input image)\" and describe the motion in \"Image to video\". The first frame is resized to width x height, so set them to the same aspect ratio as your image (multiples of 32).\n\nThe model, text encoder, VAEs, corrector, shift 12 / 3, Euler, simple schedule and 20 steps are the same as the text-to-video workflow. S3 is guidance-distilled, so it runs at CFG 1 with BasicGuider and no negative prompt.\n\nApply H3 Corrector runs on every step by default.\n  start_step / end_step: 0-based and inclusive; -1 = through the last step.\n  strength 0 turns it off.\n  budget_fraction 0.5 and velocity_floor 0.001 are what the S3 corrector was trained with.\n\nlength snaps to 17k+5 frames at 24 fps: 56 is about 2 s, 124 about 5 s.\n\nThe S3 pipeline prompts with structured JSON captions, like the example prompt. Keep the subject's appearance consistent with the input image and describe only what moves.\n\nLoadH3Corrector / ApplyH3Corrector come from S3_ComfyUI.zip in the SulphurAI/Sulphur-3 repository. To run without them, bypass both corrector nodes (Ctrl+B)."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
